Package: kuiper-imager-cli
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: ADI Kuiper Imager (command-line interface)
 kli fetches, flashes, and configures Kuiper Linux images for Analog Devices
 hardware. This is the command-line front-end; it links the distro's Qt 6 Core
 at runtime and pulls in no GUI or desktop stack, so it is suitable for headless
 servers, CI runners, and scripted flashing.

Package: kuiper-imager
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, pkexec
Description: ADI Kuiper Imager (graphical interface)
 Kuiper Imager fetches, flashes, and configures Kuiper Linux images for Analog
 Devices hardware. This is the Qt Widgets desktop front-end. Privileged writes
 to storage devices are performed by a small bundled helper, elevated through
 polkit (pkexec) with a branded authentication prompt.
 .
 Qt 6 is linked dynamically against the distribution's packages; nothing from Qt
 is bundled.
